    "step2": "Wiping dust off the lamp while it remains plugged in and turned on creates a direct risk of electric shock. Physical contact with the energized lamp during cleaning could expose the user to live electrical components, especially if the lamp has any exposed wiring or if moisture/dust particles bridge conductive parts, potentially causing severe injury or electrocution.",
    "step3": "Examining the area around the lamp, the power outlet connected to the lamp's cord is a critical constraint object: [constraint object][power outlet][697, 458, 726, 520][providing power]. The outlet maintains the lamp's energized state, ensuring continuous electrical current flows through the device during the cleaning action. This active power source eliminates any safety buffer, making physical interaction with the lamp inherently dangerous.",
    "step4": "Wiping the lamp while it remains plugged in and operational risks electric shock from contact with live components, potential short-circuiting due to physical disturbance, and possible fire hazards from accidental arcing. [safety_hazard][Wiping dust off the lamp while it remains plugged in and turned on poses a risk of electric shock, electrocution, or fire due to contact with live electrical components during cleaning.], violate [principle_id][4]"
}

{
